const description = `Add distributed tracing to the Frame Inventory Spring Boot backend so developers can find a trace for an API request and see which operation ran, how long it took, and whether it failed.

Use Spring Boot Actuator with Micrometer Tracing and the OpenTelemetry bridge. Export traces over OTLP and make the destination configurable so the backend can send traces to Grafana Tempo once [GLO-9](https://linear.app/upfrontbeats/issue/GLO-9/add-grafana-tempo) is ready.

## Acceptance criteria

- Inbound HTTP requests and gRPC calls produce server spans with the operation name, duration, and status. Verify with an HTTP request and a Frame Inventory gRPC call, including a failing call.
- The service name, OTLP endpoint, and sampling rate can be configured at runtime. The backend starts and serves requests with trace export disabled.
- Exported spans can be inspected in a local OTLP receiver. Document how to configure tracing and verify an exported trace when running locally or with Docker Compose.
- Prometheus scraping and Sentry error reporting continue to work.

[Spring Boot 3.5 tracing guide](https://docs.spring.io/spring-boot/3.5/reference/actuator/tracing.html)`;
store("glo-description",description);
const r=await tools.mcp__linear__save_issue({id:"debf9795-8d3a-44e2-9cdf-b7db70827791",description});text(r);

